#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124235 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "e1036a11-ebb3-594d-aba1-be259eb0596d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5419" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $9 \\times 11$ matrix that has $9$ pivot columns, then what is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$?" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A$.\n\nSince $A$ has $11$ columns and $9$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is\n$11-9=2$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2\n$$\n\n."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124236 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/id #uuid "4aa47a89-9f9b-55d8-ba01-a131b20e6c95" :question/math-academy-id "e-5421" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. If $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n2. If $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n3. If $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix.\n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1$.\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=2$.\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$nd column). So, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124237 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/id #uuid "42d77ab8-0670-55bf-8b99-68270c8e5f2e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5422" :question/problem "Given $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)$?" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{3} &:=R_{3} + 3R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{4} \\mid:=R_{4} + 3R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column).\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A)) = 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81e07bfb-c503-593d-b127-e0f5360ff1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121703} {:answer/id #uuid "d7469f89-bc79-5f32-9b31-5b252b4aa440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121704} {:answer/id #uuid "098ad1b8-464f-5181-9198-4030161af100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121705} {:answer/id #uuid "4460ff4e-3796-5628-adc9-b46e1e717138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121706} {:answer/id #uuid "56c36fe8-99cf-5aad-b8e7-9835640fb9c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56c36fe8-99cf-5aad-b8e7-9835640fb9c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121707} :answer-field/id #uuid "961747f3-07ef-5a2b-a1e6-a7732b196868" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121702}] :question/id #uuid "574853c6-277a-5d86-89c4-02f84dccc61a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34900" :question/problem "Let $R$ be a $8 \\cdot 12$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $R$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed2ff973-9a9f-5fa2-b687-b3f523bddec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121709} {:answer/id #uuid "0048719e-d776-5014-807d-c9c9393a8a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121710} {:answer/id #uuid "0b8521fd-5f8e-5c34-bb4b-b7bde5e34659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121711} 